# The extractor touches production data and stays untracked; the snapshots
# it writes are tracked SELECTIVELY — see the redistribution rule below.
_local_*.py
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# session notes and executor instructions for both papers — untracked
claude/
agents/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Redistribution rule for snapshots/<tag>/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TRACKED — the numbers the papers publish, and what a reader needs to verify
# them: assets.csv, betas.csv, factor_covar.csv, factor_premia.csv,
# MANIFEST.json. Small, derived, and quoted in the manuscripts.
#
# NOT TRACKED — the three return panels. They carry ~25 years of licensed index
# and factor histories (MSCI, Bloomberg, ICE BofA, HFRI, Eurekahedge) rather
# than published results, so they are not redistributed. This also restores the
# decision already taken on the identical factor-NAV content under its former
# path papers/matf_cma_jpm_2026/data/futures_risk_factors.csv, which the move
# to cma_data had silently undone.
#
# loaders.py treats every panel as OPTIONAL: it loads when present, is None when
# absent, and PaperInputs.require_panel() raises a message naming the file and
# the scripts that need it. Manifest verification hashes every file that IS
# present and reports the absent ones, so tampering is still caught on
# everything shipped. See cma_data/README.md for which scripts need which panel.
snapshots/**/asset_excess_logreturns.csv
snapshots/**/asset_total_returns.csv
snapshots/**/factor_navs.csv

# Provider CMA vectors: licensed/anonymised inputs, gated on the per-provider
# provenance confirmation (roadmap O-J7b). Pre-emptive — the file does not exist
# yet, and it must never be committed by accident when it lands.
snapshots/**/providers.csv
# the provider name map lives with the extractor and is never committed
*name_map*
